#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The committed closure corpus, written from invented data.

tests/fixtures/closure_corpus.json is generated by this file. Every
person, subject, address and id in it is invented; nothing is read from a
mailbox, a ledger or a log. The cases are built to exercise each world
kind and each signal `preprocessor/closure_harness.py` scores, in both
directions: a should_close case the signal must still close, and a
must_not_close case that reproduces the shape of a false close the signal
is now fenced against.

A corpus rebuilt from the owner's own history (scripts/build_closure_corpus.py)
is an optional, owner-private input; see `closure_harness.real_corpus_path`.

    python3 tests/fixtures/closure_corpus_synthetic.py           # write the fixture
    python3 tests/fixtures/closure_corpus_synthetic.py --check   # exit 1 when stale

`discriminating` comes from `closure_harness.py audit` over the scrubber
revisions in AUDIT_REVISIONS: a must_not_close case no scored build
closes is listed in VACUOUS, and re-running the audit after a corpus
change updates that list.
"""
